10. Elevation, Shadows, Hairlines & Dark Mode Hierarchy (Content Layer Rules)

Copycats fail in the opaque content layer because they use web CSS defaults:

1.  Two-Layer Physical Shadow Formula (Never One Dirty Blur):
      - Key Shadow: Offset downward (y > 0, e.g., y = 4..12pt), moderate blur (r
        = 12..30pt), low alpha (0.08..0.14).
      - Ambient / Contact Occlusion Shadow: Centered (y = 0..1pt), tight blur (r
        = 1..3pt), crisp grounding edge (alpha 0.04..0.08).
      - Colored Shadow Glow (Album art / Hero cards): Sample downscaled blurred
        image underneath (scale = 0.1, saturation = 1.6, opacity = 0.25..0.40,
        offsetY = 8..16pt) instead of black mud.
2.  Physical 1px Hairlines (separator): Never 1pt borders (2px or 3px
    physical!). Draw 1.0 / contentsScale (0.5pt @2x, 0.33pt @3x) at ~12% opacity
    (rgba(60,60,67,0.29) light / rgba(84,84,88,0.6) dark), inset past leading
    list icons.
3.  Grouped Canvas Inversion & Dark Mode Stepping:
      - Light Grouped: Grey canvas (#F2F2F7) behind crisp white cards (#FFFFFF)
        — the inverse of typical flat white web pages.
      - Dark Mode: Never invert colors or flatten everything to #000000. Apple
        uses semantic elevation stepping: Base (#000000 / #1C1C1E), Elevated 1
        (#1C1C1E / #2C2C2E), Elevated 2 (#2C2C2E / #3A3A3C), so modals, sheets,
        and grouped cards naturally brighten as they come closer to the user.

